{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"532ffaf1e4acfa89","type":"text","text":"# $$\\text{Parabolic}$$\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{E}{(\\mathbf{k})}=\\frac{\\hbar^{2}}{2m}\\Big( k_{x}^{2}+k_{y}^{2}+k_{z}^{2} \\Big)\n$$\n\n$$\n\\rho(\\mathcal{E}) = \\frac{4\\pi {m_e}^{3/2}}{\\hbar^3}\\sqrt{2\\mathcal{E}}\n$$","x":-1014,"y":360,"width":314,"height":290},
		{"id":"44f60da9618c95cf","type":"text","text":"# $$\\text{intraband}$$\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\infty}\nf^{T}(\\mathcal{E}+\\hbar\\omega)\\big[1-f^{T}(\\mathcal{E})\\big]\\,\n\\rho(\\mathcal{E}+\\hbar\\omega)\\, \\rho(\\mathcal{E})\\,\nd\\mathcal{E} \n$$","x":-847,"y":15,"width":487,"height":210},
		{"id":"c38c4ec82f55e5f2","type":"text","text":"# $$\\text{non-parabolic}$$\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{E}_{c}(\\mathbf{k}) = \\mathcal{E}_{0c} + \\frac{\\hbar^2 k_{\\perp}^2}{2m_{c\\perp}} - \\frac{\\hbar^2 k_{\\parallel}^2}{2m_{c\\parallel}} \n$$\n\n$$\\rho(\\mathcal{E}) = \\frac{4\\pi m_{c\\perp}\\sqrt{m_{c\\parallel}}}{\\hbar^3} \\sqrt{ 2 }\\left[ \\sqrt{ E_{cut}^{\\perp} - (\\mathcal{E} - \\mathcal{E}_{0c}) } - \\sqrt{ \\max\\Big[0, \\mathcal{E} - \\mathcal{E}_{0c}\\Big] - (\\mathcal{E} - \\mathcal{E}_{0c}) } \\right]$$","x":-649,"y":360,"width":729,"height":290},
		{"id":"d8fcfe739557b691","type":"text","text":"# $$\\text{General Emission Integral}$$\n$$\n\\Gamma(\\hbar\\omega) = \\frac{2\\pi}{\\hbar} \\left( \\frac{2V}{(2\\pi)^{3}} \\right)^{2} \\sum_{\\alpha, \\beta} \\iint\\limits_{\\text{BZ}} |\\mu^{\\alpha\\beta}(\\mathbf{k_{1}},\\mathbf{k_{2}})|^{2} \\ f_{\\alpha}(\\mathbf{k}_{1})\\overline{f_{\\beta}(\\mathbf{k}_{2})} \\ \\delta\\big(\\mathcal{E}_{\\beta}(\\mathbf{k}_{2}) - \\mathcal{E}_{\\alpha}(\\mathbf{k}_{1}) + \\hbar\\omega \\big) \\ d^{3}k_{1} \\ d^{3}k_{2} \n$$","x":-532,"y":-320,"width":875,"height":200},
		{"id":"07d3b2954850545a","type":"text","text":"Delta approximation and directly calculating in k-space proved computationally expensive and ultimately unwarranted given that a proper path into a 1D E-space integration is available","x":-277,"y":15,"width":365,"height":210},
		{"id":"5226b7820cfd36d8","type":"text","text":"# $$\\text{Interband}$$\n$$\nI(\\hbar\\omega)= \\frac{\\pi^{2}|\\mu|^{2}}{\\hbar \\sqrt{ \\overline{A}D }}\n\\int\\limits_{\\mathcal{E_{min}(\\hbar \\omega)}}^{\\mathcal{E_{max}(\\hbar \\omega)}} \\frac{{f(\\mathcal{E})f(\\hbar\\omega-\\mathcal{E})}}{\\sqrt{ \\mathcal{E_{max}(\\hbar\\omega)}-\\mathcal{E} }} \\; d\\mathcal{E}\n$$","x":160,"y":0,"width":434,"height":240},
		{"id":"5a729c7e3f3a9f85","type":"text","text":"$$\n\\mathcal{E}\\in(0,\\mathcal{E}_{\\text{max}})\n$$\nThe bottom of the parabolic band is set as 0","x":-1360,"y":413,"width":280,"height":184},
		{"id":"315f3b0fcb70427b","type":"text","text":"# $$\\text{Low Energy Approximation}$$\n$$\n\\rho^{2}(\\mathcal{E}_{F})\\,\\frac{\\hbar\\omega}{e^{\\beta\\hbar\\omega}-1}\n$$","x":-847,"y":1061,"width":527,"height":180},
		{"id":"d4a0ff81c2f99517","type":"text","text":"# $$\\text{Analytic (Const eDOS Thermal Distribution)}$$\n$$\n\\rho^{2}(\\mathcal{E}_{F}) \\frac{k_BT}{e^{\\beta\\hbar\\omega}-1}\\Big[\\beta\\hbar\\omega+\\ln\\left(1+e^{-\\beta\\mu}\\right)-\\ln\\left(1+e^{\\beta(\\hbar\\omega-\\mu)}\\right)\\Big]\n$$","x":-933,"y":800,"width":700,"height":200},
		{"id":"8437171c621730ad","type":"text","text":"here the band is a saddle and no global minimum can be set, so integration limits should be determined both from above and below","x":160,"y":415,"width":307,"height":180},
		{"id":"212330fac0498327","type":"text","text":"Measuring this against the integral on the thermal factor is a good way of understanding numeric convergence.","x":-198,"y":805,"width":286,"height":190},
		{"id":"da6c4b5aa48107f9","x":-1707,"y":800,"width":693,"height":200,"type":"text","text":"# Analytic (Const eDOS Non-Equilibrium)"}
	],
